Sh4KhE0E:=name=Memory care;disabled=1;schedule=0 3 * * *;target=paws;message=Daily memory care. Go through the shared memory regions and keep each true to its purpose, as stated in its about entry. Let finished or abandoned items fade by rating them down, and rate up entries you have verified to be correct and useful. Every rating adds to an average, so rate only while it still changes the picture: up only while the rating is below 4, down only while it is above 2. Move temporary notes that are still true to the region they belong to, merge duplicates, improve poor mnemonics, and mark entries safe where the region's description asks for it. Check entries against the current state of the platform where you can. Correct what is wrong and delete what is obsolete. A safe flag protects against expiry, not against error: clear it when an entry is false, and remove an entry only after you have verified that. When unsure, leave the entry and name it in your summary. If its creator or last editor could settle the question and the question blocks a decision, ask them with call. The reply arrives later in your personal memory, so leave the entry untouched until then. Otherwise decide yourself. Leave other users' personal regions alone and do not pass on content from private entries. Finish with a one-line summary of what you changed.
CgPSDU1r:=name=Error log check;disabled=1;schedule=30 3 * * *;target=paws;message=Daily error log check. Open the Backend's Files app (Dateien) and read /data/#log/error.txt there[chr59] direct URLs into /data/ are blocked. For each new error, first check memory whether it is already known. If not, find the cause, fix it when that is within reach and safe, and record cause, fix and verdict in memory under the error's own wording. Message the administrator only when a human decision is needed.
wUvu3zpV:=name=Full backup;disabled=1;schedule=0 2 * * 0;target=paws;message=Weekly full backup. In the Backend under System, start the backup and watch the daemon monitor on the same page until it has finished. Then open /#update/backup in the Files app and confirm that new files with today's date exist. The backup lies on this server and keeps only the previous generation. If it failed or no new files appeared, message the administrator.
opOPimOh:=name=Security check;disabled=1;schedule=0 6 * * 1;target=paws;message=Weekly security check. In the Backend's Log app, review the past week: bots flagged or blocked, requests that ended on the error page (probing for sensitive paths), the most active clients and users, and unusual traffic spikes. Check memory for what is already known or accepted, and record new findings with their verdict. Message the administrator only about something that needs a decision or action.
